From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:45:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] ufs: ufs-mediatek: make the bootloader reset SMC
 optional

The MTK_SIP_BL_UFS_CONTROL reset added for U-Boot running as the first
non-secure stage is not appropriate when the stock LK chainloads U-Boot
as a boot-image kernel. Put it behind UFS_MEDIATEK_BL_RESET, default off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/Kconfig        | 10 ++++++++++
 drivers/ufs/ufs-mediatek.c |  3 ++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/Kconfig b/drivers/ufs/Kconfig
index 6dffdc00b3..b66ab015bd 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/ufs/Kconfig
@@ -37,6 +37,16 @@ config UFS_MEDIATEK
 
 	  If unsure, say N.
 
+config UFS_MEDIATEK_BL_RESET
+	bool "Reset the UFS controller through the bootloader SMC"
+	depends on UFS_MEDIATEK
+	help
+	  Issue the bootloader-stage MTK_SIP_BL_UFS_CONTROL reset before link
+	  startup. This is needed when U-Boot replaces the vendor LK as the
+	  first non-secure stage. Leave it disabled when the vendor LK
+	  chainloads U-Boot as a boot-image kernel: LK has already owned the
+	  controller, and the kernel-stage device reset path is used instead.
+
 config UFS_PCI
 	bool "PCI bus based UFS Controller support"
 	depends on PCI && UFS
diff --git a/drivers/ufs/ufs-mediatek.c b/drivers/ufs/ufs-mediatek.c
index db60166bfd..b383a05ce7 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/ufs-mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/ufs-mediatek.c
@@ -107,7 +107,8 @@ static int ufs_mtk_pre_link(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	 * to run in non-secure world, we need to reset the UFS
 	 * controller via the SMC to acknowledge the switch.
 	 */
-	mtk_ufs_bootloader_smc_reset();
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_UFS_MEDIATEK_BL_RESET))
+		mtk_ufs_bootloader_smc_reset();
 
 	ret = ufs_mtk_unipro_set_lpm(hba, false);
 	if (ret)
